            <ArticleTitle>Evidence for an antihyperalgesic effect of venlafaxine in vincristine-induced neuropathy in rat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Venlafaxine, a new antidepressant with fewer side effects, could be of interest to reduce neuropathic pain following antineoplasic drug treatment. In the present study, we demonstrated that venlafaxine inhibits hyperalgesia in a new rat model of neuropathy induced by the antineoplasic drug vincristine, and exerts its effect preferentially via supraspinal and spinal mechanisms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
